---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="About Four Dogs Entertainment | Serving SC, NC & GA" description="Meet the Four Dogs Entertainment team and learn how we create affordable, fun hosted entertainment for events across South Carolina, North Carolina, and Georgia.">
<section class="section dark"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">About Four Dogs</p><h1>Four dogs gave us our name. People make the nights.</h1><p class="lead">A South Carolina entertainment company built around the people who show up, grab a mic, and play along.</p></div></section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container split">
    <div>
      <h2>It started with Cookie, Sammy, Boone, and Darla.</h2>
      <p>Those four dogs are the namesakes of Four Dogs Entertainment. Joey Elledge brought his event-management background and love of a good crowd into a company that hosts real nights out, not just background music.</p>
      <p>Today our team runs trivia, Music Bingo, Survey Showdown, karaoke, weddings, and private celebrations. We plan the details, bring the right host, and make sure guests know how to join the fun.</p>
      <p>Our regular public events are in South Carolina, including the Midlands and Fountain Inn. We also book weddings and private events in North Carolina and Georgia, depending on the date and location.</p>
      <p>Bring your people. We’ll bring the Doggone Good Time.</p>
      <div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/events/">Find an event</a><a href="/booking/">Book Four Dogs →</a></div>
    </div>
    <img src="/images/gallery/four-dogs-trivia-team-at-long-table.webp" alt="Four Dogs trivia guests gathered around a table at a live game night" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section alt">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="team-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">Meet the team</p>
      <h2>Meet the people on the mic.</h2>
      <p class="lead">Joey, Jim, and Elle bring different backgrounds to the same job: make the night easy to join and worth coming back for.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="team-grid">
      <article class="team-card">
        <img class="team-photo team-photo-joey" src="/images/team/joey-elledge.webp" alt="Joey Elledge, owner and host of Four Dogs Entertainment" width="500" height="718" loading="lazy">
        <div class="team-body">
          <p class="team-role">Owner &amp; Host</p>
          <h3>Joey Elledge</h3>
          <p>Joey has a background in sport and event management and is also a college professor. Four Dogs is named for Cookie, Sammy, Boone, and Darla, the four dogs who inspired the company. His vision is simple: make professional entertainment affordable, flexible, and genuinely fun for any kind of event, from a weekly game night to a wedding, private party, or company event.</p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="team-card">
        <img class="team-photo team-photo-jim" src="/images/team/jim-kennedy.webp" alt="Jim Kennedy, lead host with Four Dogs Entertainment" width="500" height="500" loading="lazy">
        <div class="team-body">
          <p class="team-role">Lead Host</p>
          <h3>Jim Kennedy</h3>
          <p>Originally from New Jersey, Jim is a musician and drummer who has played in bands. That background shows up in the way he hosts: good timing, strong crowd awareness, and the ability to keep a room moving without making the night feel forced.</p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="team-card">
        <img class="team-photo team-photo-elle" src="/images/team/elle.webp" alt="Elle, host and marketing team member with Four Dogs Entertainment" width="500" height="617" loading="lazy">
        <div class="team-body">
          <p class="team-role">Host &amp; Marketing</p>
          <h3>Elle</h3>
          <p>Originally from Florida, Elle is a musician, dog lover, and part of both the hosting and marketing side of Four Dogs. She brings creativity, energy, and an easygoing style to live events while helping shape how Four Dogs connects with people off the mic, too.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .team-intro {
    max-width: 780px;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .team-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }

  .team-card {
    background: #fff;
    border-radius: 3px;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .team-photo {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
    object-fit: cover;
    background: var(--navy);
  }

  .team-photo-joey { object-position: center 22%; }
  .team-photo-jim { object-position: center 28%; }
  .team-photo-elle { object-position: center 28%; }

  .team-body {
    padding: 1.35rem 1.4rem 1.5rem;
  }

  .team-role {
    margin: 0 0 .35rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: .1em;
    font-size: .76rem;
    font-weight: 900;
    color: var(--blue);
  }

  .team-body h3 {
    margin-bottom: .6rem;
  }

  .team-body p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 850px) {
    .team-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .team-photo {
      aspect-ratio: 5 / 4;
      object-position: center 25%;
    }
  }
</style>
</Base>
